      "text": "Since $\\sin E = 1$, we know that $\\angle E$ is a right angle.\nTherefore, $\\angle D + \\angle E = 90^\\circ$, so $\\angle D = 90^\\circ - \\angle E$.\nUsing the sine sum identity, we have $\\sin (90^\\circ - \\angle F) = \\cos \\angle F$.\nSince $\\angle D = 90^\\circ - \\angle E$, we have $\\sin D = \\cos \\angle E = \\frac{5}{13}$.\nTherefore, $\\cos \\angle F = \\cos (90^\\circ - \\angle D) = \\sin \\angle D = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{13}}$.The answer is: \\frac{12}{13}",
